---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import ConfigDemo from "../components/ConfigDemo.astro";
import { CONFIG_BASE, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";

const write = `curl -X PUT ${CONFIG_BASE}/v1/configs/checkout \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $NANO_API_KEY" -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"maintenance": false, "max_items": 50}'`;

const flip = `curl -X PATCH "${CONFIG_BASE}/v1/configs/checkout?note=incident-4711" \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $NANO_API_KEY" -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -H 'if-match: "7"' -d '{"maintenance": true}'`;

const read = `curl -s ${CONFIG_BASE}/v1/configs/checkout/keys/maintenance \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $NANO_API_KEY"
# {"name":"checkout","key":"maintenance","value":true,"version":8}`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`NanoConfig — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="A small JSON document you can change from anywhere, without a deploy. Versioned, safe for two writers, cheap to poll. Free."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="hero">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">nano-api / config</p>
					<h1>Flip the switch<br /><span class="dim">without a deploy</span></h1>
					<p class="lede">
						A small JSON document, read often and written rarely. Kill switches, feature flags,
						limits: the handful of values you should not have to redeploy to change.
					</p>
					<p class="cta">
						<a class="button" href="/howto/#setup">Take a key</a>
						<a class="button secondary" href="/howto/#config">Curl walkthrough</a>
					</p>
					<p class="fineprint muted">
						Free. Signup is one <code>curl</code> and the key comes back in the response. No form, no
						card, nobody to ask.
					</p>
				</div>
				<ConfigDemo />
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>Write it, read it</h2>
				<pre><code>{write}</code></pre>
				<p class="muted small">
					<code>PATCH</code> merges keys and <code>null</code> removes one. Read the whole document,
					or a single value when that is all you need.
				</p>
				<pre><code>{read}</code></pre>
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>Three ways I got this wrong by hand</h2>
				<ol class="steps">
					<li>
						<span class="n">1</span>
						<h3>Polling it hurts, so you poll it rarely</h3>
						<p>
							Then the kill switch takes ten minutes to reach anything. Here every read carries an
							<code>ETag</code>: send <code>If-None-Match</code> and an unchanged document answers
							<code>304</code> with no body. Check every few seconds and nobody notices.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="n">2</span>
						<h3>Two people edit, one edit disappears</h3>
						<p>
							Mid-incident that is exactly what happens: you and a colleague both fix it. Send
							<code>If-Match: "7"</code> and the write only lands if nothing moved since. The loser
							gets <code>412</code> and both version numbers, rather than silence.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="n">3</span>
						<h3>Rolling back makes v1 mean two things</h3>
						<p>
							Restore the old content and anything holding "version 1" is now wrong. So restoring
							writes that content as a <em>new</em> version instead. The number only ever goes up,
							and one version number never describes two documents.
						</p>
					</li>
				</ol>
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>The kill switch, mid-incident</h2>
				<pre><code>{flip}</code></pre>
				<p class="muted small">
					The last 20 versions are kept with the note you pass. That is what you read afterwards to
					see who flipped what, and when.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>Using it with the others</h2>
				<p>
					Keep the schedule <a href="/relay/">Relay</a> calls, the window
					<a href="/pulse/">Pulse</a> watches, and the switch that pauses both, in one document you
					can change from anywhere.
				</p>
				<p class="cta">
					<a class="button" href="/howto/">How to, in curl</a>
					<a class="button secondary" href="/about/">What this is</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.hero {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr;
		gap: 2.5em;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 2em 0 1em;
	}
	.dim {
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.lede {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		max-width: 34em;
	}
	.cta {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.7em;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		margin: 1.4em 0 0.6em;
	}
	.fineprint {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.band {
		padding: 3em 0 0;
	}
	.band > p {
		max-width: 46em;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.small {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.steps {
		list-style: none;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 1.2em;
		margin: 1.4em 0 0;
		padding: 0;
	}
	.steps li {
		border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
		padding-top: 1em;
	}
	.steps .n {
		font-family: var(--mono);
		color: var(--alive-ink);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
	}
	.steps h3 {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		margin: 0.2em 0 0.4em;
	}
	.steps p {
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.93rem;
		margin: 0;
	}
	@media (max-width: 860px) {
		.hero,
		.steps {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
